acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce each failure in its test file; classify upstream contract changes; pass focused tests, full coverage and typecheck; regenerate tracked build and changelog."
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T19:17:13.074Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Installed SDK/ops 2026.11.4 with changelog 2026.10.31 after merging current main. Changelog check already passes; do not apply the empty-window policy used by other packages. Reproducing brief.test.ts, action.test.ts and read-output-host.test.ts separately before the full coverage run. Keep prior completed fixture migrations closed."
  "2026-11-04T19:33:38.498Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Verified hosted logs and local action.test.ts: the retained-owner fixture expects claim_principal=prior-agent after close/reopen, but gets undefined. Root cause: pm-cli 2026.10.31 pm-8xgg7i intentionally clears orphan claim metadata (classification: test). Assert the exact new clear contract and preserve stale-principal/no-assignee coverage by importing a valid legacy record through commitImportedItem, then exercise unchanged previews and native start/close for both current and legacy records. Keep the live-assignee refusal controls."
  "2026-11-04T19:36:14.813Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Ownership regression passes through pm test. Six enforcement-mode/actor combinations now each exercise both a freshly reopened native record with cleared claim_principal and an SDK-imported legacy record retaining prior-agent without an assignee. Preview byte-preservation, native start/close success and live-assignee refusals remain asserted. Main brief.test.ts passed 245/245; typecheck passes; no lint script is declared."
  "2026-11-04T19:51:28.557Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"The repaired ownership regression passes on Node 22.23.4 and Node 26.13.0 (one selected test on each), as well as via pm test on Node 24.19.0. Packaged host output tests pass 13/13 and the main brief file passes 245/245. All original action-file failures were the cleared-principal assertion now replaced with both native-clear and legacy-import controls. Test compilation, production audit, typecheck and strict health pass. Full coverage remains queued."
  "2026-11-04T20:53:02.766Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Strengthened the migrated ownership regression to assert both ownership fields are cleared immediately after native close, as well as after reopen. The imported legacy record still retains prior-agent without an assignee, preserving the original stale-owner control. Updated focused case passes again on Node 22 and Node 26; test compilation passes."
  "2026-11-04T23:08:34.594Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Remaining local gate blocker: on SDK 2026.11.4 and Node 24.19.0, npm run coverage exceeded the 2400-second linked-test limit. The recorded-dependency 500-sequence model in test/handoff-coverage.test.ts and the contract/acknowledgment/renewal 500-sequence model in test/handoff-repair.test.ts each also reached its existing 900-second test deadline. Later files were interrupted, so there is no complete full-suite count or valid final coverage claim. These runtime-limit failures are not classified as SDK semantic regressions without a controlled reproduction; no production workaround, reduced sequence count, timeout increase or threshold change is applied. Diagnose the two long model cases and complete the full gate in follow-up verification. The package budget prevents another long run in this task."
  "2026-11-04T23:08:36.847Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Verified migration result: the native close/reopen ownership regression passes on Node 22 and Node 26 with both ownership fields cleared immediately after close and after reopen. A real SDK-imported legacy record retains stale principal/no-assignee controls across all six enforcement-mode/actor combinations; preview byte-preservation, native start/close and live-assignee refusals remain asserted. The main brief file passes 245/245 and packaged-host output tests pass 13/13 separately. Typecheck, test compilation, build, docstrings, production audit, workflow verification, strict health, changelog checks, publish-attestation verification and pack dry-run pass; no lint script is declared. Existing coverage thresholds remain lines 100, functions 100, branches 97.85. Push the verified pm-8xgg7i test-contract fix and leave this item in progress with full coverage incomplete."
  "2026-11-04T23:13:20.102Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Execution caveat discovered during final review: the local full-gate launcher applied nice -n 10 to pm test, while the linked command also begins nice -n 10. These increments are cumulative, yielding effective niceness 19. This launcher mistake weakens any inference from the local deadlines about SDK performance; it is not evidence of a semantic SDK regression. Correct verification recipe: launch pm test from a normal-priority shell and retain nice -n 10 only in the existing linked coverage command. No package test, deadline, sequence count, source scope or threshold needs changing. The package time budget prevents another full run here; complete the queued exact-head CI gates and, if needed, repeat local coverage with niceness applied once."
  "2026-11-05T05:04:44.508Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"Resumed from the clean Dependabot head including ecefa0d and d59ce15, on a separate fix branch for review. Verified scripts/accept-packed.ts still expects a principal after native claim-close-reopen. pm-cli 2026.10.31 pm-8xgg7i deliberately clears it; classification: test fixture contract drift, same cause as the repaired unit test. Preserve both native-clear and separately imported legacy stale-principal records across every acquisition scenario; do not remove the legacy control."
  "2026-11-05T05:42:59.940Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"The exact Bun packed command first reproduced npm-current legacy ownership fixture was not retained. The repaired sequential run has advanced past npm-current and bun-current into npm-minimum, retaining both native-clear and separately imported stale-principal controls in the packed artifact. The retained unit regression passes again through pm test (one selected test, six mode/actor combinations); typecheck, test compilation, build, docstrings and changelog checks pass. No lint script exists. Full coverage is now the only queued full suite; its original thresholds and model deadlines remain unchanged. The unpublished branch carries all earlier agent changes with inherited trees preserved during author normalization."
  "2026-11-05T06:00:16.408Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"The repaired exact Bun packed command reached its 2400-second linked-test bound. Its sequential loop completed npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum, npm-global and bun-global, then started npx-ephemeral; bunx-ephemeral was not reached and no final seven-scenario receipt exists. All assertions and all seven default scenarios remain. This is incomplete local acceptance evidence, not a green full gate or a proven SDK regression. The full npm coverage gate is still running with the original model deadlines and thresholds."
  "2026-11-05T06:19:44.828Z",codex-toolchain-1104,"At the approximately 75-minute repo budget, stopped the full npm coverage attempt after 2162 seconds, preserving PM output capture. Partial output records three unchanged test deadlines: the effective-policy severity matrix at 600000 ms and both 500-sequence handoff models at 900000 ms. There is no final test count and no valid final coverage receipt; partial LCOV is invalidated. The focused native/legacy ownership test passes and the repaired packed loop completed five acquisition scenarios before its separate 2400-second bound. These local deadline failures do not establish a new SDK semantic regression. Preserve all scenarios, assertions, model sequence counts and thresholds; publish the verified pm-8xgg7i fixture correction for exact-head CI and orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-05T09:12:30.329Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 207: fetched all review threads and comments (one unresolved: PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6z9ytC; pagination complete), and the latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range section. Branch matches remote and includes current main. Valid finding: startTask changes ownership before existing close execution. Add independent imported stale-principal direct-close fixtures across all modes and actors; inspect packed acceptance for the same sequencing gap. Preserve existing previews, start assertions, live-owner refusal controls and thresholds. Prove added coverage with an isolated stale-principal close regression, then run both full release gates. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-05T09:20:09.903Z",codex-agent,"Resolved PRRT_kwDOSzIO-c6z9ytC in code: added a separate real non-git tracker regression with six independent imported close records (none/warn/strict x two actors). Each record retains prior-agent and no assignee immediately before direct close; no startTask or claim runs on those records. Assert ready ownership-free preview, unchanged tracker snapshot, successful native close and cleared ownership. Existing start/preview cases and live-owner refusal controls are unchanged. Whole-PR self-review found the same missing direct-close execution in scripts/accept-packed.ts: added a separate stale record, JSON/TOON previews with no mutation, pre-close stale/unassigned assertions, actual installed-host close and terminal-status assertion for every one of seven acquisition scenarios. No other instance found."
  "2026-11-05T09:20:12.762Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for this test-only review finding: in a disposable code/dependency copy, injected stale-principal/no-assignee rejection into only the bundled native mutateCloseMetadata function used by the SDK. Existing ownership regression still PASSED 1/1; new independent direct-close regression FAILED 0/1 with review207_stale_principal_close_regression. Selecting the pre-fix regression alone reproduces the coverage hole. Restored both bundled SDK function copies in finally, then reran both regressions: PASSED 2/2, zero failed/skipped. No installed dependency or reviewed source was mutated for the proof. There is no changed production function to revert in this coverage-only correction."
  "2026-11-05T09:20:14.870Z",codex-agent,"Local validation: pinned pm test run of node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"native close clears ownership|direct native close\" test/action.test.ts PASSED 2/2, zero failed/skipped (six independent direct-close combinations). Typecheck, test compilation, changelog generation/check and strict health with required merge drivers pass. Full npm and Bun release commands are linked unchanged; validate the final pushed head through both CI release-gate jobs and report their exact counts. A local npm full-gate attempt uses a fresh HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration to reproduce CI identity; any shared-host timeout remains incomplete local evidence until CI passes. All model counts, deadlines, seven packed scenarios and thresholds remain unchanged: lines 100, functions 100, branches 97.85. dist is generated and ignored, with no tracked dist files. Greptile is unavailable (trial ended); skipped reviewer checks are not approval. Leave item in progress and release this claim for orchestrator verification."
